 17592186393000 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393035 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119837 1038 #edb/ref 17592186391186 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119837 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393042 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119837 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393049 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393021 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119840 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393028 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119849 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392979 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119850 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392547 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392521 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119858 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393354 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119864 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393611 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119880 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392534 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119940 1038 #edb/ref 17592186391688 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119941 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393063 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186119942 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393070 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117777 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120278 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391654 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120278 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120278 1071 "![](images/d1/d162245ac19c3ef9ae63d602fb4e188ddfd241a1a604304f6c272c3902ce1e93.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t) = ⟨\\sin 2t, \\cos 3t⟩$ from $t = 0$ to $t = π$?" 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120278 1071 "![](images/d1/d162245ac19c3ef9ae63d602fb4e188ddfd241a1a604304f6c272c3902ce1e93.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120278 1074 "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120286 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117825 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120286 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391695 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120286 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120286 1071 "Given the curve  $r(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=10t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120286 1071 "Given the curve $r(t) = 8\\cos ti + 8\\sin tj + 6tk$, $t \\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s = 10t$, find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s)$, parametrized by $s$." 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120286 1074 "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+6(\\frac{s}{10})k \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s}{5})k \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120290 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117849 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120290 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391748 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120290 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120290 1071 "Given the Cartesian equation $x - y + 4z + 16 = 0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r - p) \\cdot n = 0$." 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120290 1071 "Given the Cartesian equation $x-y+4z+16=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120290 1074 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-1,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+4z+16 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}y-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120330 1068 #edb/ref 17592186118089 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120330 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391871 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120330 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120330 1071 "Consider the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $Null(A)$." 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120330 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120330 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186118328 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391903 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120374 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120374 1071 "Consider the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$. Find the value of $k$ such that $b ∈ Null(A)$." 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120374 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120374 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3k-15 \\\\ -2+k-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3k-15=0 \\\\ k-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=5.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120429 1068 #edb/ref 17592186118658 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120429 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392468 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120429 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120429 1071 "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|=$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120429 1071 "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$?" 13194139533464 17592186045585 false] [17592186120429 1074 "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+2\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186120452 1068 #edb/ref 175921