\\\\ y=4+3t \\\\ z=-6+5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391186 1072 #uuid "aa8c997f-15c5-5b2a-b1e2-bd26aa6233d8" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391186 1074 "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-t \\\\ y=4+3t \\\\ z=-6+5t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,4,-6⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-1,3,5⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-1,3,5⟩.$ So, a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-1,3,5⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391188 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391189 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391190 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391191 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391192 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391188 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391187 1080 #uuid "54786791-8d86-5133-85dc-e9b4fbb89dbd" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391188 1081 "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=23" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391188 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391188 1084 #uuid "03f8e54c-0615-5591-b542-0b782cd89daf" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391189 1081 "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391189 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391189 1084 #uuid "de1fd91f-8a5e-51f3-8dc2-a58537f9f1b0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391190 1081 "r\\cdot ⟨-3,0,4⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391190 1084 #uuid "c540887b-e7fe-5d55-972c-cf0a8340ba96" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391191 1081 "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=⟨-3,0,4⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391191 1084 #uuid "796aa680-c468-5852-b522-12b6bd2cf262" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391192 1081 "r\\cdot ⟨-3,0,4⟩=23" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391192 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391192 1084 #uuid "eee5c6a8-ae14-524b-a64c-c15d96be1896" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391194 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1069 "q-333271" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1072 #uuid "659c7156-a7e5-547d-940d-48b6db396c6c" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391193 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=3$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]={e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/c4/c46568f3173dfeaab6e33e83269262e8692f13e245a42983ba1a9d4302ec5357.png)" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391195 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391196 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391197 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391198 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391199 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391196 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391194 1080 #uuid "2af1b5dc-48bc-57ad-a9be-047a4bcca023" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391195 1081 "images/bf/bffb2f815cc5a7db0c521054006aa834b17071f5dd33a97fe977e5d118b771be.png" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391195 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391195 1084 #uuid "aa084511-df9a-52dd-9bd1-276adcecff68" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391196 1081 "images/c4/c46568f3173dfeaab6e33e83269262e8692f13e245a42983ba1a9d4302ec5357.png" 13194