 =-2$ of multiplicity two. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$ The equilibrium point (origin) is a \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\nnode." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391225 1072 #uuid "04b55cbe-b4be-543b-bbe4-7f5a1dc7e192" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391225 1074 "The matrix of our system is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- Since the only (repeated) eigenvalue of $A$ is negative, we have a $\\text{stable}$ node.\n\n- Since $A$ is not diagonal and has a repeated eigenvalue, there is only one linearly independent eigenvector. So, we have a $\\text{degenerate}$ node.\n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/c1/c1d7f49dfe79bcd36394e4b0bb49180167ac7a8791555f0f6974f5fe49fa249f.png)" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391227 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391228 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1077 "field-2" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391228 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391226 1080 #uuid "23101e77-153a-53ab-8eaa-fb91f151bfef" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391227 1081 "star" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391227 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391227 1084 #uuid "1750bded-03a2-535d-9322-af370f69f5d0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391228 1081 "degenerate" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391228 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391228 1084 #uuid "7b95026e-9297-5fe5-b515-53db91622691" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391230 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391231 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1077 "field-1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391230 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391229 1080 #uuid "5874e815-f2f7-5127-b199-5dfa1e8dd28e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391230 1081 "stable" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391230 1084 #uuid "4552e55a-71fb-5355-a8ff-c44fe89b0c45" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391231 1081 "unstable" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391231 1084 #uuid "79852ea3-d668-55cf-ae57-0e55042a72c7" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391233 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391236 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391239 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391244 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1069 "q-333640" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1072 #uuid "d111108f-9aed-5eb7-8811-2065601ee640" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391232 1074 "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $x=0$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/0d/0d9e032bfffa68f487347d6c169999e313247e89ef7de3fae28edb216dcf718f.png)" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391234 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391235 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1077 "field-1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391235 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391233 1080 #uuid "c76521b0-e06a-5475-a7d5-6e2974a8f112" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391234 1081 "a stable" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391234 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391234 1084 #uuid "c3550c5b-1a