cc-581d-b50d-d0762931b97f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391263 1074 "The matrix of our system is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- Since the only (repeated) eigenvalue of $A$ is $\\lambda =-1$ and it's negative, we have a $\\text{stable}$ node.\n\n- Since $A$ is diagonal and has a repeated eigenvalue, there are infinitely many linearly independent eigenvectors. So, we have a $\\text{star}$ node.\n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/92/92efcce675a436ad349ca6139cb12cda88fbdd5bdeaf2a5f1e755e7ba1f6d037.png)" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391265 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391266 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1077 "field-2" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391265 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391264 1080 #uuid "91e7eaec-059c-5d14-9f8c-61c1f07a19ae" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391265 1081 "star" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391265 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391265 1084 #uuid "02a91b22-3c2e-591c-95dd-7d31a5689a08" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391266 1081 "degenerate" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391266 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391266 1084 #uuid "c3746fa1-fc10-5bb5-88e6-d4d1facc4dd2" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391268 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391269 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1077 "field-1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391268 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391267 1080 #uuid "32217f1b-d451-5dd0-8e1b-fafec5464418" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391268 1081 "stable" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391268 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391268 1084 #uuid "f0901b7b-91df-5d1e-af60-9e839083f14b" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391269 1081 "unstable" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391269 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391269 1084 #uuid "37c33283-6fbe-5f50-a58a-dfc0bc8c628a" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391271 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391276 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391281 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1069 "q-333719" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1071 "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L4}$ and substitution from lines {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1072 #uuid "49e5968a-1ea4-5510-81b8-9a383e60e6d7" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391270 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ This means that each column satisfies the differential equation. In particular, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that ${x}_{1}\\text{ is a solution of the system}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ By definition, the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column,\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}^{′}(t) & {x}_{2}^{′}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$ from $\\text{L3},$ we substitute each derivative into the matrix to get\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substitution from $\\text{L2}\\text{ and }\\text{L3}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=A[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=AΦ(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391271 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391272 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391271 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391273 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391271 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391274 13194139533464 1759