e}^{x}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391354 1072 #uuid "7cb09257-d0fc-5dab-9c6e-cd5e26a7c67a" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391354 1074 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4{y}^{2}-8{e}^{x}y+4{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=4,\\,b(x)=-8{e}^{x},\\,c(x)=4{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}=4(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-8{e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})+4{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & =4({e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z+{z}^{2})-8{e}^{x}z-8{e}^{2x}+4{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & =4{z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & =4{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =4{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =4x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{4x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{4x+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{4x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{4x+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{4x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391355 1075 #edb