en the values of $y$ and $z={y}^{′}$ at $x=1$ and asked to find their values at $x=3.$ The distance from $x=1$ to $x=3$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(1)=-2$ and $z(1)=3.$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-2$ |  |  | $3$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the first row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=3 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2x-3z}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3}{{1}^{2}}=-7 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=3\\cdot 1=3 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=-7\\cdot 1=-7 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-2+3=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=3-7=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $3$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $-7$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ |  |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the second row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=-4 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2x-3z}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-4)}{{2}^{2}}=4 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=-4\\cdot 1=-4 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=4\\cdot 1=4 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1-4=-3 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-4+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $3$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $-7$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $-4$ | $-4$ | $-4$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $-3$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(3)≈-3$\nand\n${y}^{′}(3)=z(3)≈0.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391363 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391364 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391365 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1077 "field-1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391364 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391362 1080 #uuid "09ebee1a-f1f5-5797-a0a3-8969a5355ef3" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391363 1081 "-4" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391363 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391363 1084 #uuid "91f4a159-0fa5-5fb3-9570-d38ee0ea271c" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391364 1081 "-3" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391364 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391364 1084 #uuid "a0228ec7-3203-5716-9480-7f7ee6e6a922" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391365 1081 "-2" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391365 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391365 1084 #uuid "de3cef7a-03a7-52ca-8479-785de1f38ffb" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391367 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391368 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391369 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1077 "field-2" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391366 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391368 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [1759