f 17592186391624 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391623 1069 "q-33584" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391623 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391623 1071 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(2,1,1)?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391623 1072 #uuid "93a1c03f-77b3-5fa3-b1a1-22418386cc31" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391623 1074 "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ 2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j+\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2\\,i+2(1)\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391625 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391626 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391627 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391628 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391629 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391626 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391624 1080 #uuid "3d43ad92-b445-5432-aa1f-111fa6dcfbd4" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391625 1081 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391625 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391625 1084 #uuid "9f60c71f-f1a0-5dc9-bc85-bc53e3b5d9e8" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391626 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391626 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391626 1084 #uuid "2f82adaf-7d79-546e-b51a-3d2064321d15" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391627 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391627 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391627 1084 #uuid "10b01e1d-27d8-5784-b829-e7428d99b479" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391628 1081 "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391628 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391628 1084 #uuid "8b39b63d-e746-538f-8858-f3d5381d09d5" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391629 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391629 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391629 1084 #uuid "6560a5a6-5578-53c6-881e-58e2deb05371" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186391631 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1069 "q-336341" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1071 "Consider a spherical planet with radius $(4\\times {10}^{7})\\,\\text{m}$ and surface gravitational acceleration $g=12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Which equation best models the velocity $v$ of an object projected radially outward from the planet's surface with an initial velocity of $(8\\times {10}^{4})\\,\\text{m/s},$ where $r$ is the distance from the planet's center to the object. Assume the only force acting on the object is the force due to gravity." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1072 #uuid "f3934db8-2760-5a29-9e9a-8bb1a5f5607d" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391630 1074 "Let $R$ be the planet's radius and $g$ be the planet's surface gravitational acceleration.\n\nAccording to Newton's law of universal gravitation, the magnitude of the inward gravitational force pulling the object toward the planet is\n\n$$\n{F}_{\\text{in}}=G\\,\\frac{mM}{{r}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $G$ is the gravitational constant, $m$ is the object's mass, and $M$ is the planet's mass.\n\nSince this is the only force and it acts inward, the resultant force, taking *outward* as positive, is $F=-{F}_{\\text{in}}.$\nApplying Newton's second law, $F=ma,$ where $a$ is the acceleration of the object, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =-{F}_{\\text{in}} \\\\ ma & =-G\\,\\frac{mM}{{r}^{2}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{GM}{{r}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the acceleration is inversely proportional to the square of the distance,\n\n$$\na=-\\frac{k}{{r}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwith constant of proportionality $k=GM>0.$\n\nWhen at the surface, $r=R,$ the acceleration of the object due to gravity is $a=-g.$ Substituting into our previous equation, we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n-g=-\\frac{k}{{R}^{2}}\\,\\,\\,⟹\\,k=g{R}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the equation, we get\n\n$$\na=-\\frac{g{R}^{2}}{{r}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since acceleration $a$ is the derivative of velocity $v,$ which is the derivative of distance $r,$ we can express acceleration as follows using the chain rule, treating $v$ as a function of $r$ along the trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\  & =\\frac{dr}{dt}\\cdot \\frac{dv}{dr} \\\\  & =v\\frac{dv}{dr}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result into our equation, we obtain a separable differential equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\nv\\frac{dv}{dr}=-\\frac{g{R}^{2}}{{r}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSolving using separation of variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{dv}{dr}\\,dr & =\\int (-\\frac{g{R}^{2}}{{r}^{2}})\\,dr \\\\ \\int v\\,dv & =-g{R}^{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{r}^{2}}\\,dr \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =-g{R}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{r})+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =\\frac{2g{R}^{2}}{r}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $C=2{C}_{1}$ is a constant of integration.\n\nLet ${v}_{0}$ be the initial velocity of the object. Applying the initial condition $v(R)={v}_{0},$ we can solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(R)^{2} & =\\frac{2g{R}^{2}}{R}+C \\\\ {v}_{0}^{2} & =2gR+C \\\\ C & ={v}_{0}^{2}-2gR\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation for the velocity of the object is\n\n$$\n{v}^{2}=\\frac{2g{R}^{2}}{r}+{v}_{0}^{2}-2gR.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting in the values\n$R=(4\\times {10}^{7}),$\n$g=12,$ and\n${v}_{0}=(8\\times {10}^{4}),$\nwe conclude that the equation for the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 12\\cdot (4\\times {10}^{7})^{2}}{r}+(8\\times {10}^{4})^{2}-2\\cdot 12\\cdot (4\\times {10}^{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{384\\times {10}^{14}}{r}+(64\\times {10}^{8})-(96\\times {10}^{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{r}+(6.4\\times {10}^{9})-(0.96\\times {10}^{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{r}+((6.4-0.96)\\times {10}^{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{r}+(5.44\\times {10}^{9}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391632 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391633 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391634 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391635 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1075 #edb/ref 17592186391636 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1079 #edb/ref 17592186391633 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391631 1080 #uuid "ef392484-5295-5810-8c60-385d592168de" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391632 1081 "{v}^{2}=\\frac{1.92\\times {10}^{16}}{r}-(6.4\\times {10}^{9})" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391632 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391632 1084 #uuid "e9460548-1670-5748-96e7-bc24a48140dd" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391633 1081 "{v}^{2}=\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{r}+(5.44\\times {10}^{9})" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391633 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391633 1084 #uuid "7567d868-8018-5a56-ba2a-c4d82ce4076c" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391634 1081 "{v}^{2}=\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{{r}^{2}}+(6.4\\times {10}^{9})" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391634 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391634 1084 #uuid "8d7dc8e9-09fb-5583-bb8b-d85f5b039614" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186391635 1081 "{v}^{2}=\\frac{3.84\\times {10}^{16}}{r}-(5.44\\times {10}