84 #uuid "79d86d3a-5442-5662-ab8e-bda1a724f157" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392354 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1069 "q-40293" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1071 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1072 #uuid "d52318cf-590e-555c-bafa-19ac086a5c9f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392353 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{25}{\\sqrt{26}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392355 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392356 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392357 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392358 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592