ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392421 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{1}}{‖{a}_{1}‖} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{2}}{‖{a}_{2}‖} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V=\\text{Col}(A)$ spanned by the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ of the matrix $A,$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ shown above. Given that ${a}_{1}⊥{a}_{2},$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|\\,d\\,|?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392421 1072 #uuid "d9b27ae0-730c-5147-ab83-3cb6142a7ece" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392421 1074 "Since the first two vectors are already orthogonal, we proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: We set ${v}_{2}={a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3**. Next, we find ${v}_{3}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{3}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{16}{16}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${v}_{3}$ dividing it by $‖{v}_{3}‖=\\sqrt{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{3} & =\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $|\\,d\\,|=|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392423 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392424 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392425 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392426 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392427 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1079 #edb/ref 17592186392427 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392422 1080 #uuid "c028424c-3d91-55d9-932a-ac5901ce7206" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392423 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392423 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392423 1084 #uuid "1a8a40ae-cd89-50d8-a25c-80c8f2e72194" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392424 1081 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392424 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392424 1084 #uuid "58731cd5-c497-5022-aec7-778724ff51ac" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392425 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392425 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392425 1084 #uuid "264463ee-c13b-575c-94d3-bd01355c5b9c" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [175