592186045585 true] [17592186392600 1084 #uuid "8bee35bf-0fbc-59b3-ad02-d3fba93e60a8" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392602 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1069 "q-47680" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1071 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x=-2?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1072 #uuid "7d0eb31e-00b8-5cab-baf1-ea4a71c1aca7" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392601 1074 "Notice that the function $p(x)$ is differentiable for all real number $x.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $p(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nAll other functions are not differentiable at $x=-2.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$has a vertical tangent at $x=-2$, and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=-2$ and hence it is not differentiable there." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392603 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392604 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392605 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392606 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392607 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1079 #edb/ref 17592186392607 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392602 1080 #uuid "c8ec3f96-b4f7-5beb-bf42-ca6e80ff521a" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392603 1081 "h(x)=\\sqrt[3