}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392727 1084 #uuid "e77630a7-5ba0-527b-b582-20214c8e5890" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392729 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1069 "q-50371" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1072 #uuid "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392728 1074 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392730 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392731 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392732 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392733 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392734 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1079 #edb/ref 17592186392731 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392729 1080 #uuid "03ef94ed-b793-5