ue] [17592186392824 1069 "q-62107" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392824 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392824 1071 "![](images/24/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392824 1072 #uuid "17e99f21-4a32-5f31-9b6f-4f7bf7f5a533" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392824 1074 "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](images/c3/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392826 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392827 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392828 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392829 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392830 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392825 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 1759