186045585 true] [17592186392897 1071 "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $r(t)={t}^{3}\\,i+3t\\,j+{t}^{4}\\,k$ from  $t=2$ to $t=5?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392897 1072 #uuid "93e74816-9928-5c75-b857-debb8b7d37d0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392897 1074 "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\,j+4{t}^{3}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(3)^{2}+(4{t}^{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+9+16{t}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392899 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392900 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392901 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392902 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392903 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1079 #edb/ref 17592186392899 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392898 1080 #uuid "0e4f8290-db9f-5614-851c-76e4decb0150" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392899 1081 "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392899 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392899 1084 #uuid "b393a27d-b443-5b97-b762-ed6603aad1e1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392900 1081 "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{{t}^{6}+{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392900 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392900 1084 #uuid "66fa210a-e578-5c4d-8132-eb89718f32cd" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392901 1081 "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{8{t}^{5}+9{t}^{3}+6}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392901 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392901 1084 #uuid "85f0edfc-dff0-5ee7-a4b2-955898d40c67" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392902 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392902 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392902 1084 #uuid "d8531aa7-d3a8-5834-8493-ee803adaa77f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392903 1081 "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392903 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392903 1084 #uuid "d88974de-cee3-50ec-af8b-a8554a2c05b4" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1068 #edb/ref 17592186392905 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1069 "q-64836" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1071 "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(3,1)$ where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, given that $‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖=2,$ and the unit tangent vector to the curve is $\\,T(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1072 #uuid "42a574c4-fd0d-57cc-b972-6174b753f17e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392904 1074 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨3,1⟩,$ since the point $P(3,1)$ is at the tip of $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=⟨-1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=\\frac{2}{1}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+R(\\frac{\\pi }{2})N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨3,1⟩+2⟨-1,0⟩=⟨1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392906 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392907 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392908 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392909 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392910 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1079 #edb/ref 17592186392906 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186392905 1080 #uuid "6471e1f5-248e-565f-ace6-4ec44c15f9ca" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17