ies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-13⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393030 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393031 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393032 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393033 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393034 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393034 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393029 1080 #uuid "dd843a19-122b-52dc-97b2-1085325976eb" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393030 1081 "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393030 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393030 1084 #uuid "f840eb8f-ab9a-5f24-8c61-1495e09eec29" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393031 1081 "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393031 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393031 1084 #uuid "91ee1039-c30b-5d26-b83c-09088d137cb6" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393032 1081 "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393032 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393032 1084 #uuid "23c5e4b7-8bec-5100-9926-e941a39c382d" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393033 1081 "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,7,-1⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393033 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393033 1084 #uuid "4d0de0e0-0dc6-5fa0-9f0d-4286598f473e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393034 1081 "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393034 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393034 1084 #uuid "4781d9fd-c985-5f91-b6b3-1be2153657f7" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393036 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1069 "q-70827" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1072 #uuid "ee04e6aa-94ba-5e6d-a904-4a34aac7a757" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393035 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨1,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393037 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393038 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393039 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393036 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393040 13194139533464 17592186045585 true