194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393084 1074 "The function $F(t)=f(t)\\cdot g(t)$ is differentiable over the common domain where both $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are differentiable. A vector function is differentiable if and only if each component is differentiable.\n\nLet's now find the intervals where each of the functions $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are differentiable.\n\nFor the function $f(t):$ \n\n- The first  and third components, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}$ and ${3}^{t},$ are differentiable for all values of $t.$\n\n- The second component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t)$ is differentiable on $(-\\infty ,0).$\n\nSo,  the intersection of the domains of all three components of $f(t)$ is $(-\\infty ,0).$  \n\nFor the function $g(t):$ \n\n- The first component $\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}$ is differentiable on $(-1,1)$, as its derivative is not defined at $t=\\pm 1$ and the function is not defined for $|t|>1.$\n\n- The second and third components, component $t+7$  and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ are differentiable for all values of $t.$\n\nHence,  the intersection of the domains of all three components of $g(t)$ is  $(-1,1).$    \n\nFinally, the common domain of differentiability for $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ is $(-\\infty ,0)\\cap (-1,1)=(-1,0).$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393086 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393087 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393088 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393089 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393090 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393088 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393085 1080 #uuid "690c4be0-8a71-5707-98c7-17039c45d319" 13194139533464 17592186045