 true] [17592186393125 1071 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $z=1$ and $x=y.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393125 1072 #uuid "ce5171f6-22a8-5be0-9547-0d96404368c9" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393125 1074 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $z=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=y$ (or $x-y=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393127 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393128 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393129 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393130 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393131 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393129 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393126 1080 #uuid "faddb070-9799-589d-b442-8793b0a574ea" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393127 1081 "⟨1,-1,0⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393127 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393127 1084 #uuid "5fc33413-8200-5afe-93e6-6458c7c8e9bb" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393128 1081 "⟨0,0,1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393128 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393128 1084 #uuid "a249b7e6-f321-572b-95e1-9881de3b676d" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393129 1081 "⟨1,1,0⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393129 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393129 1084 #uuid "7a095b8f-ee85-53aa-bcff-2bfe68c67e76" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393130 1081 "⟨-1,0,0⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393130 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393130 1084 #uuid "02a083d9-ebb3-54c7-86b9-863f7bd3eb31" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393131 1081 "⟨0,1,-1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393131 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393131 1084 #uuid "0401bdc3-5a0a-5673-95e9-ba3ea18f4008" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393133 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1069 "q-71270" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1071 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $y=-2$ and $x=z-1.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1072 #uuid "07f0b1a9-ab3f-550e-aed9-fa24adcc5d73" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393132 1074 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $y=-2$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=z-1$ (or $x-z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393134 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393135 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393136 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393137 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393138 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393135 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393133 1080 #uuid "0dbac2a6-bbc5-5083-88c8-9b304da962d1" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393134 1081 "⟨-1,1,-1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393134 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393134 1084 #uuid "aa0ac3f8-438f-54c7-b4f9-c594d79dd1ae" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393135 1081 "⟨-1,0,-1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393135 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393135 1084 #uuid "ee9dfc58-5aea-568f-92c8-b3bb1b22b61f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393136 1081 "⟨-1,0,1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393136 1084 #uuid "cd752dc0-22e1-56c0-97bc-d5c3b6653ad5" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393137 1081 "⟨0,1,0⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393137 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393137 1084 #uuid "a270c1dd-469b-558e-bafe-8ab31f4627af" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393138 1081 "⟨1,0,-1⟩" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393138 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393138 1084 #uuid "a3354cd6-67f4-5aec-82d5-d960556c9346" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393140 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1069 "q-71401" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=2$ gives two lines\n- $c=3$ gives a hyperbola" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1072 #uuid "89b4a109-08c5-568a-830b-41c72ba008a5" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393139 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+1 & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-2){y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curve is $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which is an ellipse.\n\nSo, only statement II is true." 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393141 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393142 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393143 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393144 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393145 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393145 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393140 1080 #uuid "fd0197e2-e874-569c-8e06-ebf5b465b2c0" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393141 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393141 1084 #uuid "06c33198-cc5c-5160-81c8-f47faca10bd5" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393142 1081 "I only" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393142 1084 #uuid "c4b91d53-b9bb-5ccd-8284-07162ce795a3" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393143 1081 "III only" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393143 1084 #uuid "cbf41b51-bd8b-557e-b601-007569be086e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393144 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393144 1084 #uuid "1f00e675-dab1-5590-88bb-52f5380183c9" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393145 1081 "II only" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393145 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393145 1084 #uuid "290fdd35-0379-5b6c-ae69-55ff1d34cf7b" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393147 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1069 "q-71413" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1071 "![](images/29/29253192bb8863030c3464dd2c42be40922db96f3de6f3e57674f2a59f862e09.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ shown above?" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1072 #uuid "d3f898f6-b08f-5687-adf4-0ea719bca50f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393146 1074 "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =c \\\\ x & =\\pm \\operatorname{arccos}⁡c+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that in the equations $x=\\pm \\operatorname{arccos}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/c5/c5ea7e325483eeb3572c90b78a5cf72040d84b98dee51a1ca2bdf4dcab5b8d2f.png)" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393148 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393149 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393150 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393151 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393152 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393150 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393147 1080 #uuid "077949f5-62c8-59b7-9b63-c9e8b3537b15" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393148 1081 "images/98/98d449048718ab75fc54a659bc74314f26b6059c5e7a7ed4af28b7edfeb69a69.png" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393148 1084 #uuid "bdd6b5d4-ea23-5caf-8777-7138860af8ce" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393149 1081 "images/a8/a8c4e910e3884ee68518752ab814f491edb14d422b4c25926b7d3ad34720592d.png" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393149 1084 #uuid "7487cd45-f801-550a-a1b4-5e2864c83b4b" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393150 1081 "images/c5/c5ea7e325483eeb3572c90b78a5cf72040d84b98dee51a1ca2bdf4dcab5b8d2f.png" 13194139533464 175921860455