3205 1084 #uuid "349c2643-543b-501a-b8d3-7af986d4a0af" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393206 1081 "images/ed/edbcc3bcef921ef736f9bd31bec56f69736c632bf835cf4c9c1c46026fda8083.png" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393206 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393206 1084 #uuid "d7836927-19a4-54a2-aabf-fc9fd48ada96" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393208 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1069 "q-72231" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1071 "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y={x}^{2}-6x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1072 #uuid "a4c40fff-4d18-5542-8848-571c276df41d" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393207 1074 "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-6)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393209 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393210 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393211 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393212 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393213 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393213 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393208 1080 #uuid "db06fc53-130e-5887-91ac-6c046aa2906d" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393209 1081 "-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393209 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393209 1084 #uuid "21689172-4d3c-58f4-ab05-b3ede303077e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393210 1081 "7\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393210 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393210 1084 #uuid "f697959f-44b8-5210-9f7e-1979d2a5ae7a" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393211 1081 "9\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393211 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393211 1084 #uuid "586238f7-2f99-5a8a-9664-756d8fb42861" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393212 1081 "6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393212 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393212 1084 #uuid "21422ed5-2d8c-51a5-ac65-50e7a6c83355" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393213 1081 "-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393213 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393213 1084 #uuid "454121d4-7104-549f-b640-3e2b0c443a68" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393215 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1069 "q-72377" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,1).$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1072 #uuid "85c3a288-e595-578f-a534-db75ed9d872f" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393214 1074 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,j \\\\  & =(2{y}^{2}+y+2)\\,i+(4xy+x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(2(1)^{2}+(1)+2)\\,i+(4(1)(1)+(1))\\,j \\\\  & =5\\,i+5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393216 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393217 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393218 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393219 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393220 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393220 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393215 1080 #uu