e function is defined by $g(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393506 1072 #uuid "71788e1c-b47b-5cdc-ab12-b5675e14b728" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393506 1074 "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 2)-2) \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393508 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393509 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393510 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393511 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393512 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393508 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393507 1080 #uuid "12fd382d-111a-5d82-8140-ebca31608a9e" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393508 1081 "{g}^{′}(