der an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-2x-6y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-2x-6y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=9-2{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(9-2{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $9-2{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j}.$" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393529 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393530 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393531 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393532 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393533 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1077 "selection" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393531 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393528 1080 #uuid "df84a140-508e-52ee-98bd-0a46d5280afa" 13194139533464 17592186045585 true] [17592186393529 1081 "{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}" 13194139533464 175921860455